               steps: [
                   "Simmer the pork in salted water for 25 to 30 minutes until just cooked through, then cool it in the liquid and slice it into thin, wide pieces.",
                   "Poach the shrimp in the same water for 2 minutes until pink, then peel them and slice each one in half lengthwise along the back.",
                   "Cook the vermicelli per the package, rinse cold, and drain very well; wet noodles make rolls that slide apart.",
                   "Whisk the hoisin, peanut butter, chili garlic sauce, and 3 tablespoons warm water into a thick dipping sauce, and top it with chopped peanuts.",
                   "Dip one rice paper sheet in warm water for 2 to 3 seconds only, until barely flexible, and lay it on a damp cutting board; it keeps softening as you build.",
                   "Lay a lettuce leaf on the lower third, then noodles, pork, and herbs. Place three shrimp halves cut-side up above the pile so they show through the finished roll.",
                   "Fold the bottom edge over the filling, fold in the sides, and roll upward firmly, tucking as you go. Repeat, keeping finished rolls apart so they do not stick.",
                   "Serve within an hour at room temperature with the peanut sauce; refrigeration turns the wrappers stiff and chewy.",
               ],
               note: "Under-soak the paper. It should still feel slightly stiff off the water; by the time you finish arranging the filling it will be perfectly soft and tacky.",
               shortcut: "Rotisserie chicken replaces the poached pork and shrimp entirely; the rolls lose their cool sweetness but come together in fifteen minutes."),
        Recipe(dishID: "vietnam-comtam", serves: 2, prepMinutes: 25, cookMinutes: 25, difficulty: 2,
               ingredients: [
