                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3 cups", item: "bean sprouts"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2", item: "yellow onion, thinly sliced"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "5 tbsp", item: "vegetable oil"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 head", item: "soft lettuce plus mint and cilantro, to wrap"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 cup", item: "nuoc cham (fish sauce, lime, sugar, water, chili)"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Whisk the rice flour, turmeric, salt, coconut milk, and water into a thin batter the texture of heavy cream, and rest it 15 minutes while you prep the fillings.",
                   "Heat 1 tablespoon of oil in a 10-inch nonstick skillet over medium-high until it shimmers; the pan must hiss loudly when batter hits or the shell will be pale and soft.",
                   "Sear a quarter of the pork and shrimp in the pan for about a minute, spreading them across one half.",
                   "Stir the batter, then pour in a thin ladleful while tilting and swirling the pan so it coats the whole surface in a thin, lacy sheet; you should hear the xeo hiss.",
                   "Scatter a handful of bean sprouts and onion over one side, cover for 1 minute to steam them, then uncover and cook 2 to 3 minutes more until the edges brown and lift.",
                   "Drizzle a little oil around the rim, slide a spatula under the empty half, and fold the crepe over the filling. Cook another minute until the underside is deeply golden and brittle.",
