                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1/2 tsp", item: "salt"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Press the tofu between paper towels under a plate for 10 minutes, then cut it into 1-inch cubes and pat them dry again; wet tofu spits and never crisps.",
                   "Heat the oil in a nonstick skillet over medium-high and fry the tofu in a single layer, turning every few minutes, until most sides are golden and puffed, 10 to 12 minutes. Set aside.",
                   "Pour off all but a tablespoon of oil, drop in the garlic and scallion whites, and stir for 30 seconds until fragrant but not browned.",
                   "Add the tomatoes and salt and cook over medium heat, mashing gently with the spoon, until they collapse into a loose, glossy sauce, 6 to 8 minutes.",
                   "Stir in the fish sauce, sugar, and 1/4 cup water, then return the tofu and simmer for 4 to 5 minutes so the fried skin drinks up the tomato.",
                   "Taste and adjust; it should be gently salty and faintly sweet, with the tomato reading brighter than rich.",
                   "Finish with the scallion greens and white pepper and serve hot over rice, spooning extra sauce over the grains.",
