                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "3/4 cup", item: "coconut cream"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tsp", item: "cornstarch"),
                   RecipeIngredient(amount: "1 tbsp", item: "toasted sesame seeds"),
               ],
               steps: [
                   "Soak the mung beans 1 hour, then simmer in water to cover until completely soft, about 20 minutes. Drain and mash with 2 tablespoons sugar and the salt into a thick paste.",
                   "Roll the mung bean paste into 12 balls the size of a large marble and set them aside; chill them briefly if they feel sticky.",
                   "Knead the glutinous rice flour with warm water, adding it gradually, until you have a smooth dough like soft playdough that does not crack when pressed. Rest 15 minutes under a towel.",
                   "Simmer the palm sugar, remaining sugar, ginger coins, and 4 cups water for 10 minutes into a thin amber syrup, and keep it hot on the back burner.",
                   "Flatten a golf-ball piece of dough into a disc, cup it in your palm, seal it around a mung bean ball with no air trapped, and roll smooth. Repeat for all twelve.",
                   "Boil the balls in a wide pot of water; they are done about a minute after they float, when the skin turns from chalky to translucent. Lift them straight into the ginger syrup.",
                   "Warm the coconut cream with the cornstarch and a pinch of salt, whisking until it barely thickens.",
                   "Serve three balls per glass, warm, with syrup ladled over, a spoonful of coconut cream, and a scatter of sesame seeds.",
               ],
               note: "Seal with no trapped air and no cracks; a pinhole lets syrup in and the ball splits in the pot. The dough should feel like an earlobe, soft but springy.",
               shortcut: "Canned sweetened red bean paste replaces the mung bean filling outright, trading the traditional flavor for zero soaking and mashing."),
